hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1668","###\n Abdullah bin Hashim narrated to us, saying: Bahz bin Asad narrated to us, saying: Yazid, who is Ibn Ibrahim al-Tustari, narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir (RA), that the Prophet (ﷺ) forbade eating onions and leeks. He (the narrator) said: \At that time"," there was no garlic in our land.\"" Then the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \""Whoever eats from this plant (gar"""
